--- WHAT SHIPPED (parity port of the web StaggerItem) ---
The web StaggerItem is an anonymous entrance wrapper: a `motion.div` whose variants animate its child in from a
faded, slightly-below resting position (`hidden = { opacity: 0, y: 15 }`) up to its final place
(`show = { opacity: 1, y: 0 }`) over the duration `useMotionPreference(350)` returns — `reduce ? 0 : 350` ms — and
which, under `prefers-reduced-motion`, sets the hidden variant itself to `{ opacity: 1, y: 0 }` so the child
renders straight in place. It reads no network data, exposes no labels/titles, and has no t() calls (the child
carries all semantics). Ported with the established AnimatedNumber/AIThinkingIndicator 3-file pattern, bound to
the shared P1/S8 reduce-motion seam (IMotionPreferenceSource, reused from AIThinkingIndicator.Source.cs); the view
performs no I/O and renders entirely from the projection:
  * StaggerItem.Model.cs      — StaggerItemRegistration (Slug "StaggerItem", automation id "stagger-item",
                                DefaultDurationMs=350, HiddenOffsetY=15, ShownOffsetY=0, HiddenOpacity=0,
                                ShownOpacity=1); the pure StaggerItemProjection (mirrors useMotionPreference: the
                                effective DurationMs/DurationSeconds collapse to 0 under reduced motion; Animate is
                                true only when motion is allowed AND duration > 0; the From* endpoints are the
                                15px/0-opacity rise when animating else the resting state — tied to Animate so a
                                non-animating wrapper renders with no flash, which is the same instant-settle the
                                web hidden variant collapses to under reduce-motion; the To* endpoints are the
                                invariant final state); and the PII-safe StaggerItemDiagnostics (emits only
                                `view.opened slug=StaggerItem`, never any user content).
  * StaggerItem.ViewModel.cs  — INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable holder over a fixed default duration + the
                                IMotionPreferenceSource; projects to StaggerItemProjection, raises Projection /
                                Animate when the user toggles reduce-motion at runtime, and unsubscribes on Dispose
                                (the web media-query listener cleanup). No UI-thread / WinUI dependency, so it is
                                Compile-linked into the headless test host.
  * StaggerItem.cs            — WinUI 3 ContentControl hosting the caller's content (the web `children`). On Loaded
                                it emits the view.opened diagnostic once and runs a one-shot Storyboard over the
                                host Opacity + a TranslateTransform.Y from the projection's From* to To* endpoints
                                (linear fade + cubic ease-out rise, the native FadeIn convention). Reduce-motion /
                                zero-duration snaps straight to the final state; a runtime reduce-motion toggle is
                                honoured (the entrance is one-shot — once settled it stays settled). Presentational
                                wrapper: it stamps the stable automation id and is exposed as a transparent Group
                                peer with no name of its own so the hosted child's semantics flow through unchanged.
                                System reduce-motion read once via Components.Motion.MotionPreference (the read-once
                                policy the peer motion-aware surfaces use).

STATES REPRODUCED (every branch renders): the web source reads NO network data and is a pure motion wrapper, so it
has no loading / empty / error / stale / offline matrix (identical to the sibling AnimatedNumber / AIThinkingIndicator
surfaces, whose logs document the same). The branches it DOES have are reproduced and tested: the full-motion
fade-and-rise (Animate=true: from opacity 0 / y 15 -> opacity 1 / y 0 over 350 ms) and the reduced-motion /
zero-duration instant settle (Animate=false: from == to == final state, no flash). Per-state snapshot values are
asserted for { 350/full, 350/reduced, 0/full, 600/full, 600/reduced }. Accessibility: stable automation id
"stagger-item"; the wrapper exposes no redundant name (transparent Group), reduce-motion honoured. Telemetry:
view.opened slug=StaggerItem (P1/S11), asserted PII-safe (slug only).

i18n (P1/S10): the web source has ZERO t() calls and renders no surface-owned strings (it is an anonymous wrapper
of arbitrary children), so there are no i18n keys to add and no English literals in the native code. Nothing to map
in the catalogue.

